-- The bar of 9(1A) and 10C(3): a period "not less than" a minimum number of months "commencing on the date on which the
-- appointment as statutory auditor ended"; the length above the minimum is "determined in standards set by the competent
-- authority" (outside the sources). Within the minimum the bar must be in the rules (JUST TRUE); after it the text does not
-- say (NOTHING), unless the standards' own period is supplied and has not run out.
GIVEN `the minimum number of months the Act requires` IS A NUMBER
      `the date the appointment ended` IS A DATE
      `the date of the proposed appointment` IS A DATE
      `the number of months determined in the standards` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 9(1A) the bar on appointment is in force on the day` MEANS
    IF `the date of the proposed appointment` LESS THAN `the date the appointment ended`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "commencing on the date on which the individual's appointment as a statutory auditor ended"
    ELSE IF `the date of the proposed appointment` LESS THAN `sch 10 para 3(2) the first day after a period of months beginning with a date` `the date the appointment ended` `the minimum number of months the Act requires`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE CONSIDER `the number of months determined in the standards`
              WHEN JUST k THEN
                  IF `the date of the proposed appointment` LESS THAN `sch 10 para 3(2) the first day after a period of months beginning with a date` `the date the appointment ended` k
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): what follows the standards' own period is not in the Act
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "determined in standards set by the competent authority"

