GIVEN `the sanction is a temporary prohibition of up to three years preventing a person responsible for a breach from exercising specified functions in a firm eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor or in a public interest entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is no longer a member of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 12(4) the sanction applies to the person as it applies to members` MEANS
    IF `the sanction is a temporary prohibition of up to three years preventing a person responsible for a breach from exercising specified functions in a firm eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor or in a public interest entity`
       AND `the person is no longer a member of the body`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The sanctions referred to in sub-paragraph (3)(b)(v)"

-- src:20244 | (5) The information to be made available to the public under sub-paragraph (3)(c) must include the following information (which the body must continue to make available in accordance with sub-paragraph (7)) in relation to sanctions the body imposes—
-- src:20245 | (a) information concerning the type of contravention and its nature;
-- src:20246 | (b) the identity of the person sanctioned, unless any of the circumstances mentioned in sub-paragraph (6) applies; and
-- src:20247 | (c) where a sanction is subject to appeal, information concerning the status and outcome of any appeal.
@ref sch 10 para 12(5) The information to be made available to the public about sanctions (src:20244-20247)
GIVEN `the information includes the type of contravention and its nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a circumstance mentioned in sub-paragraph (6) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information includes the identity of the person sanctioned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sanction is subject to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information includes the status and outcome of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 12(5) the information made available to the public includes what it must include` MEANS
    IF    `the information includes the type of contravention and its nature`
       AND (`a circumstance mentioned in sub-paragraph (6) applies` OR `the information includes the identity of the person sanctioned`)
       AND ((NOT `the sanction is subject to appeal`) OR `the information includes the status and outcome of the appeal`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must include the following information"

-- src:20248 | (6) The circumstances in which the identity of the person sanctioned must not be made available to the public are—
-- src:20249 | (a) where that person is an individual and the body considers the publication of personal data would be disproportionate;
-- src:20250 | (b) where publication would jeopardise the stability of financial markets;
-- src:20251 | (c) where publication would jeopardise an ongoing criminal investigation; and
-- src:20252 | (d) where publication would cause disproportionate damage to any institution or individual involved.
@ref sch 10 para 12(6) The circumstances in which the identity of the person sanctioned must not be made available (src:20248-20252)
GIVEN `the person is an individual and the body considers the publication of personal data would be disproportionate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `publication would jeopardise the stability of financial markets` IS A BOOLEAN
      `publication would jeopardise an ongoing criminal investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `publication would cause disproportionate damage to any institution or individual involved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 12(6) the identity of the person sanctioned must not be made available to the public` MEANS
    IF    `the person is an individual and the body considers the publication of personal data would be disproportionate`
       OR `publication would jeopardise the stability of financial markets`
       OR `publication would jeopardise an ongoing criminal investigation`
       OR `publication would cause disproportionate damage to any institution or individual involved`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the identity of the person sanctioned, unless any of the circumstances mentioned in sub-paragraph (6) applies" (12(5)(b))

-- src:20254 | (8) In sub-paragraph (7), “the relevant date” means—
-- src:20255 | (a) where the body imposes a sanction and that decision is appealed, the date on which the appeal is determined;
-- src:20256 | (b) where the body imposes a sanction and that decision is not appealed, the date by which any appeal was required to be lodged.
@ref sch 10 para 12(8) "the relevant date" (src:20254-20256)
GIVEN `the body imposes a sanction and that decision is appealed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the appeal is determined` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date by which any appeal was required to be lodged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`sch 10 para 12(8) the relevant date` MEANS
    IF `the body imposes a sanction and that decision is appealed`
    THEN `the date on which the appeal is determined`
    ELSE JUST `the date by which any appeal was required to be lodged`

-- src:20253 | (7) Information in relation to sanctions mentioned in sub-paragraph (3) must continue to be made available for a proportionate period and must be published on the body’s website for at least five years after the relevant date.
@ref sch 10 para 12(7) Information about sanctions must continue to be published for at least five years after the relevant date (src:20253-20253)
GIVEN `the relevant date` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 12(7) the information must be published on the website of the body on the day` MEANS
    IF `the day asked about` GREATER THAN `the relevant date`
       AND `the day asked about` AT MOST `sch 10 para 3(2) the first day after a period of months beginning with a date` `the relevant date` 60
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for at least five years after the relevant date" (after that, "a proportionate period" is not defined)

-- ---- paragraph 13: Monitoring of audits ----

-- src:20258 | 13 (1) The body must—
-- src:20259 | (a) have adequate arrangements for enabling the performance by its members of statutory audit functions to be monitored by means of inspections, where functions relating to the monitoring of the audits are the subject of a delegation of tasks to the body under regulation 3 of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016;
-- src:20260 | (b) in the case of members of the body who perform any statutory audit functions in respect of audits where functions relating to the monitoring of the audits are not the subject of such a delegation—
-- src:20261 | (i) have arrangements for the monitoring of those audits by the competent authority in accordance with those Regulations and, in respect of public interest entities, Article 26 of the EU Audit Regulation ; and
-- src:20262 | (ii) have rules and practices designed to ensure that a sanction imposed by the competent authority in accordance with those Regulations is to be treated as if it were a sanction which the body had determined under arrangements for enforcement within paragraph 12;
-- src:20263 | (c) in the case of members of the body who perform any third country audit functions—
-- src:20264 | (i) have arrangements for the monitoring of those audits by the competent authority in accordance with the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016; and
-- src:20265 | (ii) have rules and practices designed to ensure that a sanction imposed by the competent authority in accordance with those Regulations is to be treated as if it were a sanction which the body had determined under arrangements for enforcement within paragraph 12; and
-- src:20266 | (d) have rules designed to ensure that members of the body take such steps as may reasonably be required of them to enable their performance of any statutory audit functions or third country audit functions to be monitored by means of inspections.
@ref sch 10 para 13(1) Monitoring of audits: arrangements (src:20258-20266)
GIVEN `monitoring functions relating to the audits of members are the subject of a delegation of tasks to the body under regulation 3 of the 2016 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has adequate arrangements for enabling the performance by its members of statutory audit functions to be monitored by means of inspections` IS A BOOLEAN
      `members of the body perform statutory audit functions in respect of audits where functions relating to the monitoring of the audits are not the subject of such a delegation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has arrangements for the monitoring of those audits by the competent authority in accordance with the 2016 Regulations and, in respect of public interest entities, Article 26 of the EU Audit Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `members of the body perform statutory audit functions in respect of audits where functions relating to the monitoring of the audits are not the subject of such a delegation (rules limb)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has rules and practices designed to ensure that a sanction imposed by the competent authority is treated as if it were a sanction the body had determined under arrangements for enforcement within paragraph 12` IS A BOOLEAN
      `members of the body perform any third country audit functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has arrangements for the monitoring of those audits by the competent authority in accordance with the 2016 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `members of the body perform any third country audit functions (rules limb)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has rules and practices designed to ensure that a sanction imposed by the competent authority in respect of third country audit functions is treated as if it were a sanction the body had determined under arrangements for enforcement within paragraph 12` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has rules designed to ensure that members of the body take such steps as may reasonably be required of them to enable their performance of any statutory audit functions or third country audit functions to be monitored by means of inspections` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 13(1) the body meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF (    (NOT `monitoring functions relating to the audits of members are the subject of a delegation of tasks to the body under regulation 3 of the 2016 Regulations`)
             OR `the body has adequate arrangements for enabling the performance by its members of statutory audit functions to be monitored by means of inspections`)
       AND (    (NOT `members of the body perform statutory audit functions in respect of audits where functions relating to the monitoring of the audits are not the subject of such a delegation`)
             OR `the body has arrangements for the monitoring of those audits by the competent authority in accordance with the 2016 Regulations and, in respect of public interest entities, Article 26 of the EU Audit Regulation`)
       AND (    (NOT `members of the body perform statutory audit functions in respect of audits where functions relating to the monitoring of the audits are not the subject of such a delegation (rules limb)`)
             OR `the body has rules and practices designed to ensure that a sanction imposed by the competent authority is treated as if it were a sanction the body had determined under arrangements for enforcement within paragraph 12`)
       AND (    (NOT `members of the body perform any third country audit functions`)
             OR `the body has arrangements for the monitoring of those audits by the competent authority in accordance with the 2016 Regulations`)
       AND (    (NOT `members of the body perform any third country audit functions (rules limb)`)
             OR `the body has rules and practices designed to ensure that a sanction imposed by the competent authority in respect of third country audit functions is treated as if it were a sanction the body had determined under arrangements for enforcement within paragraph 12`)
       AND `the body has rules designed to ensure that members of the body take such steps as may reasonably be required of them to enable their performance of any statutory audit functions or third country audit functions to be monitored by means of inspections`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The body must—"

-- src:20267 | (2) Any monitoring of members of the body under the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016 or Article 26 of the EU Audit Regulation is to be regarded (so far as their performance of statutory audit functions, or of third country audit functions, is concerned) as monitoring of compliance with the body’s rules for the purposes of paragraph 12(1) and (1A).
@ref sch 10 para 13(2) Monitoring under the Regulations is regarded as monitoring of compliance with the rules of the body (src:20267-20267)
