-- src:20290 | (d) the remuneration received by the person in respect of statutory audit work.
@ref sch 10 para 13(7) The assessment an inspection must include (src:20286-20290)
GIVEN `the inspection includes an assessment of the compliance of the person with the standards set by the competent authority under the 2016 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inspection includes an assessment of the resources allocated by the person to statutory audit work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inspection is in relation to a firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inspection includes an assessment of the internal quality control system of the firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inspection includes an assessment of the remuneration received by the person in respect of statutory audit work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 13(7) the body meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the inspection includes an assessment of the compliance of the person with the standards set by the competent authority under the 2016 Regulations`
       AND `the inspection includes an assessment of the resources allocated by the person to statutory audit work`
       AND (    (NOT `the inspection is in relation to a firm`)
             OR `the inspection includes an assessment of the internal quality control system of the firm`)
       AND `the inspection includes an assessment of the remuneration received by the person in respect of statutory audit work`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The inspection must include an assessment of"

-- src:20291 | (8) The inspection must be appropriate and proportionate in view of the scale and complexity of the statutory audit work of the person subject to inspection.
@ref sch 10 para 13(8) The inspection must be appropriate and proportionate (src:20291-20291)
GIVEN `the inspection is appropriate and proportionate in view of the scale and complexity of the statutory audit work of the person subject to inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 13(8) the body meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the inspection is appropriate and proportionate in view of the scale and complexity of the statutory audit work of the person subject to inspection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The inspection must be appropriate and proportionate"

-- src:20292 | (9) Where undertaking inspections of statutory audits of undertakings that qualify as small (see sections 382 and 383) or medium sized (see sections 465 and 466) the body must take account of the fact that the standards determined by the competent authority under the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016 are designed to be applied in a manner that is proportionate to the scale and complexity of the business of the audited person.
@ref sch 10 para 13(9) Inspections of small or medium sized undertakings: proportionality of the standards (src:20292-20292)
GIVEN `s 382 the company qualifies as small` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 383 Companies qualifying as small: parent companies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 465 the company qualifies as medium-sized` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 466 Companies qualifying as medium-sized: parent companies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the body takes account of the fact that the standards determined by the competent authority are designed to be applied in a manner proportionate to the scale and complexity of the business of the audited person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 13(9) the body has taken account of the proportionality of the standards` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the undertaking qualifies as small or medium sized`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the body takes account of the fact that the standards determined by the competent authority are designed to be applied in a manner proportionate to the scale and complexity of the business of the audited person`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the body must take account of the fact"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "undertakings that qualify as small (see sections 382 and 383) or medium sized (see sections 465 and 466)"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): sections 382, 383, 465 and 466 (coa8, coa10) decide whether the undertaking qualifies
    WHERE
        `the undertaking qualifies as small or medium sized` MEANS
            IF    (`s 382 the company qualifies as small` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
               OR (`s 383 Companies qualifying as small: parent companies` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
               OR (`s 465 the company qualifies as medium-sized` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
               OR (`s 466 Companies qualifying as medium-sized: parent companies` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE IF    (`s 382 the company qualifies as small` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
                    AND (`s 383 Companies qualifying as small: parent companies` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
                    AND (`s 465 the company qualifies as medium-sized` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
                    AND (`s 466 Companies qualifying as medium-sized: parent companies` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
                 THEN JUST FALSE
                 ELSE NOTHING

-- src:20293 | (10) An inspection conducted in relation to a firm may be treated as an inspection of all individuals responsible for statutory audit work on behalf of that firm, if the firm has a common quality assurance policy with which each such individual is required to comply.
@ref sch 10 para 13(10) An inspection of a firm may be treated as an inspection of all individuals responsible for the audit work (src:20293-20293)
GIVEN `the inspection is conducted in relation to a firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the firm has a common quality assurance policy with which each individual responsible for statutory audit work on behalf of the firm is required to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 13(10) the inspection of the firm may be treated as an inspection of all individuals responsible` MEANS
    IF `the inspection is conducted in relation to a firm`
       AND `the firm has a common quality assurance policy with which each individual responsible for statutory audit work on behalf of the firm is required to comply`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the firm has a common quality assurance policy with which each such individual is required to comply"

-- src:20294 | (11) The main conclusions of the inspection must be recorded in a report which is made available to—
-- src:20295 | (a) the person to whom the inspection relates, and
-- src:20296 | (b) the body.
@ref sch 10 para 13(11) The report of the inspection (src:20294-20296)
GIVEN `the main conclusions of the inspection are recorded in a report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report is made available to the person to whom the inspection relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report is made available to the body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 13(11) the body meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the main conclusions of the inspection are recorded in a report`
       AND `the report is made available to the person to whom the inspection relates`
       AND `the report is made available to the body`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The main conclusions of the inspection must be recorded in a report which is made available to"

-- src:20297 | (12) The body must, at least once in every calendar year, deliver to the Secretary of State a summary of the results of inspections conducted under this paragraph.
@ref sch 10 para 13(12) A summary of inspections is delivered to the Secretary of State at least once in every calendar year (src:20297-20297)
GIVEN `the body has delivered to the Secretary of State in the calendar year a summary of the results of inspections conducted under this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 13(12) the body has complied for the calendar year` MEANS
    IF `the body has delivered to the Secretary of State in the calendar year a summary of the results of inspections conducted under this paragraph`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The body must, at least once in every calendar year, deliver to the Secretary of State a summary of the results of inspections"

-- ---- paragraphs 14 to 20ZA ----

-- src:20299 | 14 The rules and practices of the body relating to—
-- src:20300 | (a) the admission and expulsion of members,
-- src:20301 | (b) the grant and withdrawal of eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor by the body, where this task has been delegated to the body by the competent authority under regulation 3 of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016, and
-- src:20302 | (c) the enforcement action the body takes in respect of its members, where tasks related to the competent authority’s responsibility for imposing and enforcing sanctions have been delegated to the body under that regulation,
-- src:20303 | must be fair and reasonable and include adequate provision for appeals.
@ref sch 10 para 14 Membership, eligibility and enforcement: fair and reasonable, with appeals (src:20299-20303)
GIVEN `the rules and practices of the body relating to the admission and expulsion of members are fair and reasonable and include adequate provision for appeals` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the task of granting and withdrawing eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor has been delegated to the body by the competent authority under regulation 3 of the 2016 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rules and practices of the body relating to the grant and withdrawal of eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor are fair and reasonable and include adequate provision for appeals` IS A BOOLEAN
      `tasks related to the competent authoritys responsibility for imposing and enforcing sanctions have been delegated to the body under that regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rules and practices of the body relating to the enforcement action it takes in respect of its members are fair and reasonable and include adequate provision for appeals` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 14 the body meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the rules and practices of the body relating to the admission and expulsion of members are fair and reasonable and include adequate provision for appeals`
       AND (    (NOT `the task of granting and withdrawing eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor has been delegated to the body by the competent authority under regulation 3 of the 2016 Regulations`)
             OR `the rules and practices of the body relating to the grant and withdrawal of eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor are fair and reasonable and include adequate provision for appeals`)
       AND (    (NOT `tasks related to the competent authoritys responsibility for imposing and enforcing sanctions have been delegated to the body under that regulation`)
             OR `the rules and practices of the body relating to the enforcement action it takes in respect of its members are fair and reasonable and include adequate provision for appeals`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be fair and reasonable and include adequate provision for appeals"

-- src:20305 | 15 (1) The body must have effective arrangements for the investigation of complaints against—
-- src:20306 | (a) persons who are eligible under its rules for appointment as a statutory auditor, and
-- src:20307 | (b) the body in respect of matters arising out of its functions as a supervisory body.
@ref sch 10 para 15(1) Investigation of complaints (src:20305-20307)
GIVEN `the body has effective arrangements for the investigation of complaints against persons eligible under its rules for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has effective arrangements for the investigation of complaints against the body in respect of matters arising out of its functions as a supervisory body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 15(1) the body meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the body has effective arrangements for the investigation of complaints against persons eligible under its rules for appointment as a statutory auditor`
       AND `the body has effective arrangements for the investigation of complaints against the body in respect of matters arising out of its functions as a supervisory body`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The body must have effective arrangements for the investigation of complaints against"

-- src:20308 | (2) The arrangements mentioned in sub-paragraph (1) must make provision for the whole or part of the function of investigating those complaints to be performed by the competent authority under the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016.
@ref sch 10 para 15(2) Complaints: performance by the competent authority (src:20308-20308)
GIVEN `the arrangements make provision for the whole or part of the function of investigating those complaints to be performed by the competent authority under the 2016 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 15(2) the body meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the arrangements make provision for the whole or part of the function of investigating those complaints to be performed by the competent authority under the 2016 Regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The arrangements mentioned in sub-paragraph (1) must make provision for the whole or part of the function of investigating those complaints to be performed by the competent authority"

-- src:20310 | 16 (1) The body must have rules and practices designed to ensure that, where the competent authority has decided that any particular enforcement action should be taken against a member of the body following the conclusion of an investigation under the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016, that decision is to be treated as if it were a decision made by the body in enforcement proceedings against the member.
@ref sch 10 para 16(1) Independent investigation: a decision of the competent authority is treated as a decision of the body (src:20310-20310)
GIVEN `the competent authority has decided that particular enforcement action should be taken against a member of the body following the conclusion of an investigation under the 2016 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has rules and practices designed to ensure that that decision is treated as if it were a decision made by the body in enforcement proceedings against the member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 16(1) the body meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF (    (NOT `the competent authority has decided that particular enforcement action should be taken against a member of the body following the conclusion of an investigation under the 2016 Regulations`)
             OR `the body has rules and practices designed to ensure that that decision is treated as if it were a decision made by the body in enforcement proceedings against the member`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The body must have rules and practices designed to ensure that, where the competent authority has decided that any particular enforcement action should be taken against a member of the body"

-- src:20311 | (2) The body must have adequate arrangements as part of its rules and practices—
-- src:20312 | (a) to facilitate the conduct of investigations into non-delegated cases by the competent authority in connection with the performance of statutory audit functions or third country audit functions by members of the body;
-- src:20313 | (b) for the holding by the competent authority of hearings relating to members of the body in accordance with the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016, where necessary following those investigations; and
-- src:20314 | (c) for making decisions by the competent authority following those investigations as to whether (and, if so, what) enforcement action should be taken against members of the body.
@ref sch 10 para 16(2) Independent investigation: arrangements (src:20311-20314)
GIVEN `the body has adequate arrangements as part of its rules and practices to facilitate the conduct of investigations into non-delegated cases by the competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has adequate arrangements as part of its rules and practices for the holding by the competent authority of hearings relating to members of the body where necessary following those investigations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has adequate arrangements as part of its rules and practices for making decisions by the competent authority following those investigations as to whether and if so what enforcement action should be taken against members of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 16(2) the body meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the body has adequate arrangements as part of its rules and practices to facilitate the conduct of investigations into non-delegated cases by the competent authority`
       AND `the body has adequate arrangements as part of its rules and practices for the holding by the competent authority of hearings relating to members of the body where necessary following those investigations`
       AND `the body has adequate arrangements as part of its rules and practices for making decisions by the competent authority following those investigations as to whether and if so what enforcement action should be taken against members of the body`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The body must have adequate arrangements as part of its rules and practices"

-- src:20315 | (3) “Non-delegated cases” means matters relating to tasks which have not been delegated to the body by the competent authority under regulation 3 of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016.
@ref sch 10 para 16(3) "Non-delegated cases" (src:20315-20315)
GIVEN `the matter relates to a task which has not been delegated to the body by the competent authority under regulation 3 of the 2016 Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 16(3) the matter is a non-delegated case` MEANS
    IF `the matter relates to a task which has not been delegated to the body by the competent authority under regulation 3 of the 2016 Regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Non-delegated cases” means matters relating to tasks which have not been delegated"

-- src:20317 | 16A (1) The body must have adequate rules and practices designed to ensure that a person eligible under its rules for appointment as a statutory auditor transfers audit working papers and investigation reports to a third country competent authority only in accordance with the requirements of—
-- src:20318 | (a) paragraph 16AA (transfer to approved third country competent authority), or
-- src:20319 | (b) paragraph 16AB (transfer for purposes of investigation).
@ref sch 10 para 16A(1) Transfer of papers to third countries (src:20317-20319)
GIVEN `the body has adequate rules and practices designed to ensure that a person eligible under its rules for appointment as a statutory auditor transfers audit working papers and investigation reports to a third country competent authority only in accordance with paragraph 16AA or paragraph 16AB` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 16A(1) the body meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the body has adequate rules and practices designed to ensure that a person eligible under its rules for appointment as a statutory auditor transfers audit working papers and investigation reports to a third country competent authority only in accordance with paragraph 16AA or paragraph 16AB`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The body must have adequate rules and practices designed to ensure that a person eligible under its rules for appointment as a statutory auditor transfers audit working papers and investigation reports to a third country competent authority only in accordance with"

@ref sch 10 para 16A(1) A transfer may be made only in accordance with paragraph 16AA or 16AB (src:20317-20319)
GIVEN `the transfer is in accordance with the requirements of paragraph 16AA` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is in accordance with the requirements of paragraph 16AB` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 16A(1) the person may transfer audit working papers and investigation reports to the third country competent authority` MEANS
    IF (`the transfer is in accordance with the requirements of paragraph 16AA` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the transfer is in accordance with the requirements of paragraph 16AB` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (`the transfer is in accordance with the requirements of paragraph 16AA` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`the transfer is in accordance with the requirements of paragraph 16AB` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only in accordance with the requirements of"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 1253E and the other seams may not be known

-- src:20320 | (2) The body must also have adequate rules and practices designed to ensure that a person eligible under its rules for appointment as a statutory auditor must refuse to transfer audit working papers and investigation reports to a third country competent authority if the Secretary of State directs under section 1253E(6) that such a transfer should not take place.
@ref sch 10 para 16A(2) The person must refuse to transfer if the Secretary of State directs that the transfer should not take place (src:20320-20320)
GIVEN `s 1253E Working arrangements for transfer of papers: the Secretary of State directs under subsection (6) that the transfer should not take place` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 16A(2) the person must refuse to transfer audit working papers and investigation reports to the third country competent authority` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1253E Working arrangements for transfer of papers: the Secretary of State directs under subsection (6) that the transfer should not take place`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the Secretary of State directs under section 1253E(6)"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 1253E (coa27)

-- src:20322 | 16AA The requirements of this paragraph are that—
-- src:20323 | (a) the transfer is to an approved third country competent authority, and
-- src:20324 | (b) ... the Secretary of State has approved the transfer.
@ref sch 10 para 16AA Transfer to an approved third country competent authority (src:20322-20324)
GIVEN `the transfer is to an approved third country competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has approved the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 16AA the requirements of this paragraph are met` MEANS
    IF `the transfer is to an approved third country competent authority` AND `the Secretary of State has approved the transfer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The requirements of this paragraph are that"

-- src:20326 | 16AB (1) The requirements of this paragraph are that—
-- src:20327 | (a) the transfer to the third country competent authority is made for the purposes of an investigation of an auditor or audit firm, and
-- src:20328 | (b) the following conditions are met.
-- src:20329 | (2) The first condition is that the authority has requested the audit working papers and investigation reports for the purposes of an investigation which has been initiated by itself or another third country competent authority established in the same third country.
-- src:20330 | (3) The second condition is that the audit working papers and investigation reports relate to audits of companies that—
-- src:20331 | (a) have issued securities in that third country, or
-- src:20332 | (b) form part of a group issuing statutory consolidated accounts in that third country.
-- src:20333 | (4) The third condition is that, where the authority has made the request for the audit working papers and investigation reports directly to the statutory auditor, the authority has given the Secretary of State advance notice of the request, indicating the reasons for it.
-- src:20334 | (5) The fourth condition is that the authority has entered into arrangements with the Secretary of State in accordance with section 1253E.
@ref sch 10 para 16AB Transfer for purposes of investigation of auditor (src:20326-20334)
GIVEN `the transfer to the third country competent authority is made for the purposes of an investigation of an auditor or audit firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority has requested the audit working papers and investigation reports for the purposes of an investigation initiated by itself or by another third country competent authority established in the same third country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the audit working papers and investigation reports relate to audits of companies that have issued securities in that third country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the audit working papers and investigation reports relate to audits of companies that form part of a group issuing statutory consolidated accounts in that third country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority made the request for the papers directly to the statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority gave the Secretary of State advance notice of the request indicating the reasons for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1253E the authority has entered into arrangements with the Secretary of State` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 16AB the requirements of this paragraph are met` MEANS
    IF NOT (    `the transfer to the third country competent authority is made for the purposes of an investigation of an auditor or audit firm`
            AND `the authority has requested the audit working papers and investigation reports for the purposes of an investigation initiated by itself or by another third country competent authority established in the same third country`
            AND (    `the audit working papers and investigation reports relate to audits of companies that have issued securities in that third country`
                  OR `the audit working papers and investigation reports relate to audits of companies that form part of a group issuing statutory consolidated accounts in that third country`)
            AND ((NOT `the authority made the request for the papers directly to the statutory auditor`) OR `the authority gave the Secretary of State advance notice of the request indicating the reasons for it`))
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The requirements of this paragraph are that"
    ELSE `s 1253E the authority has entered into arrangements with the Secretary of State`


-- src:20320 | (2) The body must also have adequate rules and practices designed to ensure that a person eligible under its rules for appointment as a statutory auditor must refuse to transfer audit working papers and investigation reports to a third country competent authority if the Secretary of State directs under section 1253E(6) that such a transfer should not take place.
@ref sch 10 para 16A(2) Transfer refused where the Secretary of State directs (src:20320-20320)
GIVEN `the body has adequate rules and practices designed to ensure that a person eligible under its rules must refuse to transfer audit working papers and investigation reports to a third country competent authority if the Secretary of State directs under section 1253E(6) that the transfer should not take place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 16A(2) the body meets the requirement that the person must refuse` MEANS
    IF `the body has adequate rules and practices designed to ensure that a person eligible under its rules must refuse to transfer audit working papers and investigation reports to a third country competent authority if the Secretary of State directs under section 1253E(6) that the transfer should not take place`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The body must also have adequate rules and practices designed to ensure that"

-- src:20336 | 17 (1) The body must have adequate rules or arrangements designed to ensure that persons eligible under its rules for appointment as a statutory auditor take such steps as may reasonably be expected of them to secure that they are able to meet claims against them arising out of statutory audit work.
@ref sch 10 para 17(1) Meeting of claims arising out of audit work (src:20336-20336)
GIVEN `the body has adequate rules or arrangements designed to ensure that persons eligible under its rules for appointment as a statutory auditor take such steps as may reasonably be expected of them to secure that they are able to meet claims against them arising out of statutory audit work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 17(1) the body meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the body has adequate rules or arrangements designed to ensure that persons eligible under its rules for appointment as a statutory auditor take such steps as may reasonably be expected of them to secure that they are able to meet claims against them arising out of statutory audit work`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The body must have adequate rules or arrangements designed to ensure that persons eligible under its rules for appointment as a statutory auditor take such steps"

-- src:20337 | (2) This may be achieved by professional indemnity insurance or other appropriate arrangements.
@ref sch 10 para 17(2) This may be achieved by professional indemnity insurance or other appropriate arrangements (src:20337-20337)
GIVEN `the person has professional indemnity insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has other arrangements that are appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 17(2) the person is able to meet claims arising out of statutory audit work` MEANS
    IF `the person has professional indemnity insurance` OR `the person has other arrangements that are appropriate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "This may be achieved by professional indemnity insurance or other appropriate arrangements"

-- src:20339 | 18 The body must have rules requiring persons eligible under its rules for appointment as a statutory auditor to comply with any obligations imposed on them by—
-- src:20340 | (a) requirements under section 1224 (Secretary of State's power to call for information);
-- src:20341 | (b) regulations under section 1239 (the register of auditors);
-- src:20342 | (c) regulations under section 1240 (information to be made available to the public).
@ref sch 10 para 18 Register of auditors and other information to be made available (src:20339-20342)
GIVEN `the body has rules requiring persons eligible under its rules for appointment as a statutory auditor to comply with any obligations imposed on them by requirements under section 1224` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has rules requiring persons eligible under its rules for appointment as a statutory auditor to comply with any obligations imposed on them by regulations under section 1239` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has rules requiring persons eligible under its rules for appointment as a statutory auditor to comply with any obligations imposed on them by regulations under section 1240` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 18 the body meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the body has rules requiring persons eligible under its rules for appointment as a statutory auditor to comply with any obligations imposed on them by requirements under section 1224`
       AND `the body has rules requiring persons eligible under its rules for appointment as a statutory auditor to comply with any obligations imposed on them by regulations under section 1239`
       AND `the body has rules requiring persons eligible under its rules for appointment as a statutory auditor to comply with any obligations imposed on them by regulations under section 1240`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The body must have rules requiring persons eligible under its rules for appointment as a statutory auditor to comply with any obligations imposed on them by"

-- src:20344 | 19 The body must have satisfactory arrangements for taking account, in framing its rules, of the cost to those to whom the rules would apply of complying with those rules and any other controls to which they are subject.
