    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The body must have satisfactory arrangements for taking account, in framing its rules, of the cost"

-- src:20346 | 20 The body must be able and willing—
-- src:20347 | (a) to promote and maintain high standards of integrity in the conduct of statutory audit work, and
-- src:20348 | (b) to co-operate, by the sharing of information and otherwise, with the Secretary of State and any other authority, body or person having responsibility in the United Kingdom for the qualification, supervision or regulation of auditors.
@ref sch 10 para 20 Promotion and maintenance of standards (src:20346-20348)
GIVEN `the body is able and willing to promote and maintain high standards of integrity in the conduct of statutory audit work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is able and willing to co-operate, by the sharing of information and otherwise, with the Secretary of State and any other authority, body or person having responsibility in the United Kingdom for the qualification, supervision or regulation of auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 20 the body meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the body is able and willing to promote and maintain high standards of integrity in the conduct of statutory audit work`
       AND `the body is able and willing to co-operate, by the sharing of information and otherwise, with the Secretary of State and any other authority, body or person having responsibility in the United Kingdom for the qualification, supervision or regulation of auditors`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The body must be able and willing"

-- src:20350 | 20ZA (1) This paragraph applies where, under regulation 3 of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016, the competent authority has delegated the task of approving persons as eligible for appointment as statutory auditors to a body (“B”).
-- src:20351 | (2) B must pay the costs incurred by—
-- src:20352 | (a) the competent authority in carrying out activities mentioned in paragraphs 9 to 10C, 12, 13 and 16, or
-- src:20353 | (b) another recognised supervisory body, in carrying out those activities as a result of the competent authority delegating a task to the other body,
-- src:20354 | in relation to any statutory auditor bound by B’s rules.
@ref sch 10 para 20ZA Supplementary: funding of arrangements (src:20350-20354)
GIVEN `the competent authority has delegated to the body under regulation 3 of the 2016 Regulations the task of approving persons as eligible for appointment as statutory auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs were incurred by the competent authority, or by another recognised supervisory body as a result of the competent authority delegating a task to it, in carrying out activities mentioned in paragraphs 9 to 10C, 12, 13 and 16` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs are in relation to a statutory auditor bound by the rules of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has paid the costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 20ZA the body has paid the costs it must pay` MEANS
    IF    `the competent authority has delegated to the body under regulation 3 of the 2016 Regulations the task of approving persons as eligible for appointment as statutory auditors`
       AND `the costs were incurred by the competent authority, or by another recognised supervisory body as a result of the competent authority delegating a task to it, in carrying out activities mentioned in paragraphs 9 to 10C, 12, 13 and 16`
       AND `the costs are in relation to a statutory auditor bound by the rules of the body`
    THEN IF `the body has paid the costs`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "B must pay the costs incurred by"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This paragraph applies where ... the competent authority has delegated the task of approving persons as eligible"

-- ---- paragraph 20A: Interpretation (the defined terms) ----

-- src:20357 | “the Audit Directive” means Directive 2006/43/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council on statutory audits of annual accounts and consolidated accounts, amending Council Directives 78/660/EEC and 83/349/EEC and repealing Council Directive 84/253/EEC;
@ref sch 10 para 20A(1) "the Audit Directive" (src:20357-20357)
GIVEN `the instrument is Directive 2006/43/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council on statutory audits of annual accounts and consolidated accounts, amending Council Directives 78/660/EEC and 83/349/EEC and repealing Council Directive 84/253/EEC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 20A(1) the instrument is the Audit Directive` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is Directive 2006/43/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council on statutory audits of annual accounts and consolidated accounts, amending Council Directives 78/660/EEC and 83/349/EEC and repealing Council Directive 84/253/EEC`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the Audit Directive” means Directive 2006/43/EC"

-- src:20358 | “audit reporting requirements” has the meaning given by regulation 2 of the Statutory Auditors and Third Country Auditors Regulations 2016 as amended from time to time;
