-- src:20359 | “EEA auditor” means an individual or firm approved in accordance with the Audit Directive by an EEA competent authority to carry out audits of annual accounts or consolidated accounts required by European Union law;
@ref sch 10 para 20A(1) "EEA auditor" (src:20359-20359)
GIVEN `the person is an individual or firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is approved in accordance with the Audit Directive by an EEA competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the approval is to carry out audits of annual accounts or consolidated accounts required by European Union law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 20A(1) the person is an EEA auditor` MEANS
    IF    `the person is an individual or firm`
       AND `the person is approved in accordance with the Audit Directive by an EEA competent authority`
       AND `the approval is to carry out audits of annual accounts or consolidated accounts required by European Union law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“EEA auditor” means an individual or firm approved in accordance with the Audit Directive"

-- src:20360 | “EEA competent authority” means a competent authority within the meaning of Article 2(10) of the Audit Directive of an EEA State;
@ref sch 10 para 20A(1) "EEA competent authority" (src:20360-20360)
GIVEN `the body is a competent authority within the meaning of Article 2(10) of the Audit Directive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a competent authority of an EEA State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 20A(1) the body is an EEA competent authority` MEANS
    IF `the body is a competent authority within the meaning of Article 2(10) of the Audit Directive` AND `the body is a competent authority of an EEA State`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“EEA competent authority” means a competent authority within the meaning of Article 2(10) of the Audit Directive of an EEA State"

-- src:20361 | “issuer” has the same meaning as in Part 6 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (see section 102A(6));
@ref sch 10 para 20A(1) "issuer" (src:20361-20361)
GIVEN `section 102A(6) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000: the person is an issuer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 20A(1) the person is an issuer` MEANS
    `section 102A(6) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000: the person is an issuer` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) when that Act is not among the sources

-- src:20362 | “key audit partner” means—
-- src:20363 | (a) an individual who is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor and who is designated by an audit firm for a particular audit engagement as being primarily responsible for carrying out the statutory audit on behalf of the audit firm;
-- src:20364 | (b) in the case of a group audit, any of the following—
-- src:20365 | (i) an individual who is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor and who is designated by an audit firm as being primarily responsible for carrying out the statutory audit of the consolidated accounts of the group on behalf of the audit firm;
-- src:20366 | (ii) an individual who is eligible to conduct the audit of the accounts of any material subsidiary undertaking and who is designated as being primarily responsible for that audit; or
-- src:20367 | (c) an individual who is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor and who signs the audit report.
@ref sch 10 para 20A(1) "key audit partner" (src:20362-20367)
GIVEN `the individual is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is designated by an audit firm for a particular audit engagement as being primarily responsible for carrying out the statutory audit on behalf of the audit firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the audit is a group audit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is designated by an audit firm as being primarily responsible for carrying out the statutory audit of the consolidated accounts of the group on behalf of the audit firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is eligible to conduct the audit of the accounts of any material subsidiary undertaking and is designated as being primarily responsible for that audit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual signs the audit report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 20A(1) the individual is a key audit partner` MEANS
    IF `the individual is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor`
       AND (    `the individual is designated by an audit firm for a particular audit engagement as being primarily responsible for carrying out the statutory audit on behalf of the audit firm`
             OR (    `the audit is a group audit`
                 AND (    `the individual is designated by an audit firm as being primarily responsible for carrying out the statutory audit of the consolidated accounts of the group on behalf of the audit firm`
                       OR `the individual is eligible to conduct the audit of the accounts of any material subsidiary undertaking and is designated as being primarily responsible for that audit`))
             OR `the individual signs the audit report`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“key audit partner” means—"

-- src:20368 | “public interest entity” means—
-- src:20369 | (a) an issuer whose transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market;
-- src:20370 | (b) a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 of the European Parliament and of the Council, which is a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation;
-- src:20371 | (c) a person who would be an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC of 19 December 1991 of the European Parliament and of the Council on the annual accounts and consolidated accounts of insurance undertakings as that Article had effect immediately before IP completion day, were the United Kingdom a member State;
@ref sch 10 para 20A(1) "public interest entity" (src:20368-20371)
GIVEN `the person is an issuer whose transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 which is a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person would be an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC as that Article had effect immediately before IP completion day were the United Kingdom a member State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 20A(1) the person is a public interest entity` MEANS
    IF    `the person is an issuer whose transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market`
       OR `the person is a credit institution within the meaning given by Article 4(1)(1) of Regulation (EU) No. 575/2013 which is a CRR firm within the meaning of Article 4(1)(2A) of that Regulation`
       OR `the person would be an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 2(1) of Council Directive 91/674/EEC as that Article had effect immediately before IP completion day were the United Kingdom a member State`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“public interest entity” means—"

-- src:20372 | “specified state” means one of the states specified in Schedule 1 to the Recognition of Professional Qualifications and Implementation of International Recognition Agreements (Amendment) Regulations 2023;
@ref sch 10 para 20A(1) "specified state" (src:20372-20372)
GIVEN `Schedule 1 to the Recognition of Professional Qualifications and Implementation of International Recognition Agreements (Amendment) Regulations 2023: the state is one of the states specified` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 20A(1) the state is a specified state` MEANS
    `Schedule 1 to the Recognition of Professional Qualifications and Implementation of International Recognition Agreements (Amendment) Regulations 2023: the state is one of the states specified` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) when those Regulations are not among the sources

-- src:20373 | “specified state auditor” means an individual who is eligible to conduct audits of the accounts of bodies corporate that are incorporated or formed under the law of a specified state in accordance with the law of that state;
@ref sch 10 para 20A(1) "specified state auditor" (src:20373-20373)
GIVEN `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is eligible to conduct audits of the accounts of bodies corporate that are incorporated or formed under the law of a specified state in accordance with the law of that state` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 20A(1) the person is a specified state auditor` MEANS
    IF `the person is an individual` AND `the individual is eligible to conduct audits of the accounts of bodies corporate that are incorporated or formed under the law of a specified state in accordance with the law of that state`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“specified state auditor” means an individual who is eligible to conduct audits"

-- src:20375 | “statutory audit function” means any function performed as a statutory auditor;
@ref sch 10 para 20A(1) "statutory audit function" (src:20375-20375)
GIVEN `the function is performed as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 20A(1) the function is a statutory audit function` MEANS
    IF `the function is performed as a statutory auditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“statutory audit function” means any function performed as a statutory auditor"

-- src:20376 | “third country audit function” means any function related to the audit of a UK-traded third country company or of a body corporate whose transferable securities are admitted to trading on a regulated market situated or operating in an equivalent third country or transitional third country; and
@ref sch 10 para 20A(1) "third country audit function" (src:20376-20376)
GIVEN `the function is related to the audit of a UK-traded third country company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the function is related to the audit of a body corporate whose transferable securities are admitted to trading on a regulated market situated or operating in an equivalent third country or transitional third country` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 20A(1) the function is a third country audit function` MEANS
    IF    `the function is related to the audit of a UK-traded third country company`
       OR `the function is related to the audit of a body corporate whose transferable securities are admitted to trading on a regulated market situated or operating in an equivalent third country or transitional third country`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“third country audit function” means any function related to the audit of"

-- src:20378 | (2) For the purposes of this Schedule, Gibraltar is to be treated as if it were an EEA State and subject to the Audit Directive.
@ref sch 10 para 20A(2) Gibraltar is treated as if it were an EEA State (src:20378-20378)
GIVEN `the territory is Gibraltar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 20A(2) the territory is treated as an EEA State and subject to the Audit Directive for the purposes of this Schedule` MEANS
    IF `the territory is Gibraltar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Gibraltar is to be treated as if it were an EEA State"
